 "mechanism": "grouped_multi_expert_operand_residency",
 "production_or_evaluation_duration_consumed": false,
 "schema": "grouped_multi_expert_operand_residency_reference_v1",
 "why_independent_axes": "The two production fused-MoE tile signatures on these targets are BM16/BN32/BK64/GSM1 and BM64/BN64/BK32/GSM8, so BM, BK and GSM are perfectly collinear in production data. A prior single-expert probe moved BM, BN, BK and GSM independently but held one weight matrix with every tile full. This probe moves the remaining structural axes alone: the number of distinct weight matrices, the partition of M tiles among them, the N extent, the K depth, tile raggedness, and the distinct footprint under a fixed reference order."
}
